Pillar 1 — Integrity: The data you analyze must be provably identical to the data on the original device. This is achieved through cryptographic hashing.  
Integrity means ensuring that digital evidence has not been altered during collection, transfer, or analysis. 
Investigators must be able to prove that the analyzed data is exactly the same as the data originally stored on the device.
Compare the Hashes
Item	SHA-256 Hash
Original Drive	A1B3F56C99...EFF00
Forensic Image	A1B3F56C99...EFF00

The hashes are identical.

That proves:

The forensic image is an exact copy.
No data changed during acquisition.
The evidence integrity is preserved.
